# P2P protocols (Envy)

## Treat the network as hostile (hard rules)
- Validate sizes, bounds, and types before parsing.
- Reject malformed/oversized packets safely (no crashes, no allocations based on untrusted sizes).
- Never trust remote-provided paths/names: prevent traversal and invalid characters.

## Timeouts + responsiveness
- All sockets must have sane send/recv timeouts.
- Never block the UI thread on network I/O.
- Handle partial sends/receives and transient errors (`WSAEWOULDBLOCK`, `WSAEINTR`) correctly.

## Rate limiting + resource caps
- Apply rate limiting where appropriate (per-peer and/or global).
- Cap memory growth from peer-controlled inputs (queues, buffers, message maps).

## Compatibility
- Preserve backward compatibility: gate new behavior behind capability/version detection.
- Unknown/extra fields: ignore safely when possible; never assume a fixed layout.
